    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1180">

                <pb facs="1260" n="1164" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg1164"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hoshí to Mr. Day.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Japan</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-07-19"><hi rendition="#italic">July 19,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 38.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 15th instant, suggesting that, in view of avoiding all risk
                    of error or mischance, due regard should be paid to the usual naval observances
                    by neutral men-of-war which may wish to enter or to depart from any blockaded
                    port in Cuba and in Porto Rico, as well as any other ports that are now or may
                    hereafter be blockaded by the United States during the war with Spain.</p>
                <p>In reply I beg to state that I have taken due note of the contents of your
                    communication, and will not fail to notify the authorities concerned.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Toru Hoshí.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
